  "worked_solution": "First, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-2.7<X<2.7) & =0.4108 \\\\ 2P(0<X<2.7) & =0.4108 \\\\ P(0<X<2.7) & =0.2054 \\\\ P(X<2.7)-P(X<0) & =0.2054 \\\\ P(X<2.7)-0.5 & =0.2054 \\\\ P(X<2.7) & =0.7054 \\\\ P(X\\le 2.7) & =0.7054\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2.7) & =0.7054 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{2.7-0}{\\sigma }) & =0.7054 \\\\ \u03a6(\\frac{2.7}{\\sigma }) & =0.7054 \\\\ \\frac{2.7}{\\sigma } & ={\u03a6}^{-1}(0.7054)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\n\u03a6(0.54)=0.7054\\,\u21d2\\,{\u03a6}^{-1}(0.7054)=0.54.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2.7}{\\sigma } & =0.54 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{2.7}{0.54} \\\\ \\sigma  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
